; ============================================================================================
; BT-9b. SIGNAGE, BACKING PLATE -- the half that actually buys the distance. (2026-08-28.)
;
; USE THIS UNDER `label_lit.tres`, ALWAYS. Glyphs alone were the defect, not the brightness.
;
; WHY A PLATE IS THE FIX FOR "READS AT 8 m, NEEDS 20 m". Legibility at distance is contrast
; against the BACKDROP, and floating glyphs have no fixed backdrop -- the same sign is read
; against a pale ground, a bright day sky, a mid-grey connector and a black night within one
; walk around it. At 8 m the glyph strokes still cover enough pixels to win against most of
; those; at 20 m each stroke is a couple of pixels wide, it blends with whatever is behind it,
; and no amount of extra emission fixes a contrast ratio that keeps changing sign. Adding
; brightness was the wrong axis, which is why 3, 12 and 40 all produced the same complaint.
;
; A plate makes the backdrop a CONSTANT. Light glyphs on this plate are 17.6:1 (WCAG AAA is
; 7:1), and since both this file and `label_lit.tres` are UNSHADED, that ratio does not move
; with the cycle, the ambient floor, the canopy, or anything else. The sign reads the same at
; midnight as at noon because neither surface is lit at all.
;
; IT IS DARK, NOT BLACK, ON PURPOSE. Pure black plates read as holes punched in the world --
; at night an unshaded 0.0 surface is the only thing on screen darker than the sky. L* 4.0 sits
; just above the level's darkest natural surface (the lake's silt at L* ~22 is well above it,
; and the night sky is below it), so the plate reads as an object rather than as an absence.
;
; SCOPE, AND WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX. The 20 m criterion has a second, independent blocker that
; is not a material and is not this packet's: `Hub.tscn`'s `SectionLabel` carries
; `no_depth_test = true`, so an ~11 m "HUB" quad paints over the counter board from every
; viewpoint 20 m out (BT-8's capture 03). No palette can be seen through geometry that draws on
; top of everything. That is a .tscn edit and belongs to BT-5 or BT-13.
;
; Also unshaded, so it ignores EMISSION -- see the note in `label_lit.tres`.
; ============================================================================================
[gd_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" format=3]

[resource]
resource_name = "label_backing (BT-9b signage)"
shading_mode = 0
albedo_color = Color(0.055, 0.055, 0.062, 1)
cull_mode = 2
